00:19:04.820 --> 00:19:06.903
And I'm going to tell it--
that -o yaml basically

00:19:06.903 --> 00:19:08.820
says the result that
you're going to send back

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:11.010
to me that usually would
be JSON just put it

00:19:11.010 --> 00:19:13.740
out as yaml on screen so
we can see what it's doing.

00:19:13.740 --> 00:19:17.970
So we can run that, and that's
going to basically give us

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:18.840
back an allocation.

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:20.700
And the bit that we care
